---
title: Basque cheesecake
servings: 8
tags: [spanish, vegetarian, gluten-free, make-ahead]
cuisine: spanish
time: 1 hour 5 minutes
source: Adapted from Basque Burnt Cheesecake in 2xAA/cookbook (MIT), https://raw.githubusercontent.com/2xAA/cookbook/main/public/recipes/Basque%20Burnt%20Cheesecake.cook
---

Heat the oven to 200°C (400°F).

Beat the @cream cheese{600%g}(full-fat) in a #large bowl{} until smooth, then
beat in the @granulated sugar{180%g}.

Add the @eggs{4}(large) one at a time, mixing each in fully before the next.

Mix in the @vanilla extract{2%tsp} and @cornstarch{2%tbsp}, then the
@heavy cream{300%ml}, until smooth.

Grease a #round cake tin{} and line it with plenty of #parchment paper{},
leaving a generous overhang all round to hold the batter as it rises.

Pour in the batter. Bake ~{40%minutes} for a lighter cake or ~{50%minutes} for
a denser one, checking from 30 minutes. The top should be well browned and the
middle still wobbly; it sets as it cools.

Turn the oven off and leave the cake inside with the door open to cool. Then
chill at least ~{4%hours}, better overnight.

> The source gives no tin size; a 20 to 23 cm (8 to 9 inch) springform holds
> this amount.
